  "2026-10-17T09:13:24.509Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: reproduce missing dependency created_at against current checkout, preserve valid persisted-format semantics and use a typed actionable read/validation result. Bundled with pm-gh1481/pm-gh1486; all other backlog items remain unclaimed."
  "2026-10-17T09:38:49.727Z","harness:codex","Compatibility correction from the broad regression suite: existing actionable-get-receipts deliberately supports timestamp-free legacy dependencies. The final fix will preserve those rows and sort absent timestamps deterministically; typed item_document_invalid is reserved for invalid supplied timestamps. The initial strict-absence attempt is superseded, and the existing regression controls are retained."
  "2026-10-17T09:57:02.459Z","harness:codex","Corrected boundary proof passes: all 181 focused tests, including timestamp-free legacy read contracts and the safe/unsafe source-mutant controls. The same final read-context suite fails all three cases on isolated baseline eeeaf3ececc4fc18c6c41cf3c4a5d3218e92a0aa under the same updated dependencies. Missing timestamps remain absent and sort deterministically; null/numeric/invalid supplied timestamps return typed field diagnostics and validation/health expose corruption without rewriting source bytes."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T09:30:38.660Z","harness:codex","Dependency created_at is canonical write provenance, but timestamp-free legacy persisted rows already have an explicit supported read/omission contract. Validate a sorting fix against actionable-get-receipts before strengthening read-time schema validation; absence must not acquire an invented timestamp."
