body: "## Observed (pm 2026.10.15; also on 2026.10.14)\n\nA dependency row with only `id` and `kind` (no `created_at`) makes `pm get` crash with an unhandled TypeError:\n\n```console\n$ pm update rp-xhnl --dep \"id=rp-138k,kind=blocks\" --dep \"id=rp-ono1,kind=related\"\n# then the dependency table in tasks/rp-xhnl.toon is reduced to\n#   dependencies[2]{id,kind}:\n#     rp-138k,blocks\n#     rp-ono1,related\n$ pm get rp-xhnl\nCannot read properties of undefined (reading 'localeCompare')\n$ pm list --limit 5     # still works\n$ pm validate           # no check flags the malformed dependency rows\n```\n\nSupplying `created_at` on each dependency makes the item readable again. A single dependency row without `created_at` does not crash; two or more do. That suggests the dependency sort compares `created_at` with `localeCompare` without guarding against `undefined`.\n\n## How agents hit this\n\nDependency rows written by imports, by hand-edited `.toon` files, by other implementations of the format, or by older tools can lack `created_at`. pm-rust's differential suite hit it with fixture items, and pm-rust now has to keep timestamps in every fixture row to work around it. For an agent, the failure is opaque: no item id, no field name, no recovery hint, and `pm validate` reports nothing.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Reading an item never crashes on a missing optional dependency field. Sort with a stable fallback, for example by `created_at` when present, then `kind`, then `id`.\n- Or, if `created_at` is meant to be required, `pm validate` / `pm health` names the item and dependency rows. Reads then fail with a typed, actionable error that has a recovery command, not a TypeError."
